WEBVTT

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:14.660
Promises are the standard way to handle
asynchronous tasks in JavaScript,

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:17.260
moving us away from messy callback
functions.

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:21.980
A promise is an object that stands in for
a future result.

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:26.300
The fundamental shift is that functions
now return this object immediately,

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:29.500
and you attach your success or failure
logic to it later.

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:31.660
The difference is striking.

00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:36.040
Callback hell forces deep nesting and
repetitive error handling.

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:38.480
The promise chain flattens the logic,

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:41.780
allowing you to catch all errors in one
place at the end.
